  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Management program for the conservation of the recently rediscovered Hula painted frog latoni nigriventer</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will aim to fill the gap in knowledge on this prominent rediscovered living animal by gathering data on its natural history. Fundamental information is required for development of a conservation management plan in the Hula reserve, and for the establishment of a breeding program for this species. These actions are expected to push this unique species away from the brink of extinction and extend its distribution into the recently re-flooded areas of the Hula Valley. Specific objectives include: (1) defining the current distribution of the Hula painted frog; (2) Defining the population size of the Hula painted frog; (3) Defining population structure; (4) Defining preferred habitat.</narrative>
  </description>
